, {"given": "Tao", "family": "Yu", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "29733", "event": {"name": "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37", "theme": "38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024)", "location": "Vancouver, BC, Canada", "acronym": "NeurIPS 2024", "number": "37", "start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 10]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 15]]}}, "container-title": ["Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 19]], "date-time": "2026-06-19T15:44:39Z", "timestamp": 1781883879000}, "score": 50.82942, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.proceedings.com/079017-3421.html"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.52202/079017-3421", "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T14:14:37Z", "timestamp": 1785334477662, "version": "3.55.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 1]], "date-time": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1767225600000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://www.uspto.gov/ip-policy/copyright-policy/copyright-basics"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>This paper examines workflow transformation in agentic artificial intelligence for data science. The central question is: How do agentic systems change the division of labor across problem framing, data preparation, modeling, validation, and communication? We argue that the important shift is not that language models can write isolated snippets of code, but that agentic systems can bind intent clarification, tool use, iterative execution, error recovery, evidence synthesis, and stakeholder-facing explanation into one operational loop. This creates economic value by reducing coordination costs and expanding analytical capacity, yet it also changes the risk profile of data work: mistakes become more procedural, more compositional, and sometimes harder to detect. We develop a framework that treats the agent as an accountable analytical operator, evaluate implications for organizations, and propose design principles for robust deployment.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.6937638", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T13:53:47Z", "timestamp": 1785333227000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["From Copilot to Coworker: How LLM Agents Reshape End-to-End Data Science Workflows"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8977-2660", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Eledu", "family": "Shah", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 29]], "date-time": "2026-07-29T13:53:47Z", "timestamp": 1785333227000}, "score": 37.970444, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=6937638"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6937638", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 19]], "date-time": "2026-03-19T12:19:35Z", "timestamp": 1773922775181, "version": "3.50.1"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Instats Inc.", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>This workshop introduces Agentic Data Analytics, the next frontier in research automation. Unlike standard chatbots, autonomous AI agents can plan, execute, debug, and summarize an entire scientific analysis \u2014 and even draft the report. Using the free Google Antigravity tool, participants learn how to build reproducible agentic workflows using precise natural language, covering data cleaning, analysis, visualization, and report generation directly on their laptop.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.61700/85oqxe1omy90e2487", "type": "report", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 19]], "date-time": "2026-03-19T08:10:49Z", "timestamp": 1773907849000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Agentic Data Analytics: Automating Research Workflows"], "prefix": "10.61700", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1907-9700", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Peter", "family": "Gruber", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "47853", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 19]], "date-time": "2026-03-19T08:10:49Z", "timestamp": 1773907849000}, "score": 33.297283, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://instats.org/seminar/agentic-data-analytics-automating-resear"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.61700/85oqxe1omy90e2487", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 26]], "date-time": "2025-06-26T04:04:33Z", "timestamp": 1750910673252, "version": "3.41.0"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "ScienceTech Xplore", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["IJAIDSML"], "DOI": "10.63282/3050-9262.ijaidsml-v5i2p102", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 25]], "date-time": "2025-06-25T09:25:21Z", "timestamp": 1750843521000}, "page": "9-16", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Automating Data Engineering Workflows with AI and Machine Learning"], "prefix": "10.63282", "volume": "5", "author": [{"given": "Aditya", "family": "Banerjee", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "52640", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "container-title": ["International Journal of Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, and Machine Learning"], "original-title": ["English"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 25]], "date-time": "2025-06-25T09:25:23Z", "timestamp": 1750843523000}, "score": 32.841164, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://ijaidsml.org/index.php/ijaidsml/article/view/55"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.63282/3050-9262.ijaidsml-v5i2p102", "ISSN": ["3050-9262"], "issn-type": [{"value": "3050-9262", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 1]], "date-time": "2025-08-01T08:40:07Z", "timestamp": 1754037607479, "version": "3.41.2"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Madison Academic Press", "issue": "1", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["AETR"], "abstract": "<jats:p>This paper presents a comprehensive overview of the evolution of data science from a statistics-centric discipline to a machine learning\u2013driven field, culminating in the current integration of large language models (LLMs). It identifies key limitations in traditional LLM applications\u2014such as limited cross-domain adaptability, lack of interpretability, and workflow rigidity\u2014and explores recent innovations addressing these challenges. Three representative frameworks\u2014R&amp;D-Agent, SPIO, and Agent Laboratory\u2014illustrate LLMs\u2019 transition from assistive tools to autonomous agents capable of planning, executing, and optimizing entire data science workflows. These systems leverage dual-agent cooperation, modular architectures, and self-correcting capabilities to improve performance in end-to-end data analysis and scientific research. The paper concludes by outlining future priorities, including domain-specific customization, standardized agent evaluation, and improved interpretability, all of which are essential for the next generation of intelligent, autonomous data science systems.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.56028/aetr.14.1.1582.2025", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 1]], "date-time": "2025-08-01T07:55:12Z", "timestamp": 1754034912000}, "page": "1582", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["From Assistants to Agents: The Evolution of Large Language Models in Data Science Workflows"], "prefix": "10.56028", "volume": "14", "author": [{"given": "Xiyuan", "family": "Yin", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "35028", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 26]]}, "container-title": ["Advances in Engineering Technology Research"], "link": [{"URL": "https://admin.madison-publishing.com/index.php/aetr/article/download/3939/3961", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://admin.madison-publishing.com/index.php/aetr/article/download/3939/3961", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 1]], "date-time": "2025-08-01T08:04:20Z", "timestamp": 1754035460000}, "score": 31.159431, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://madison-proceedings.com/index.php/aetr/article/view/3939"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 26]]}, "references-count": 0, "journal-issue": {"issue": "1", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2025, 8, 27]]}}, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.56028/aetr.14.1.1582.2025", "ISSN": ["2790-1688"], "issn-type": [{"value": "2790-1688", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 26]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 26]], "date-time": "2026-02-26T18:52:28Z", "timestamp": 1772131948714, "version": "3.50.1"}, "description": "Supplemental Information for 10.1021/acssynbio.5c00261", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "American Chemical Society (ACS)", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.1021/acssynbio.5c00261.s001", "type": "component", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 10, 14]], "date-time": "2025-10-14T11:50:50Z", "timestamp": 1760442650000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["StreptoCAD: An Open-Source Software Toolbox Automating Genome Engineering Workflows in Streptomycetes"], "prefix": "10.1021", "member": "316", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11, 21]], "date-time": "2025-11-21T08:44:45Z", "timestamp": 1763714685000}, "score": 30.575489, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://pubs.acs.org/doi/suppl/10.1021/acssynbio.5c00261/suppl_file/sb5c00261_si_001.pdf"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1021/acssynbio.5c00261.s001", "relation": {"is-component-of": [{"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.1021/acssynbio.5c00261", "asserted-by": "object"}]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 14]], "date-time": "2026-08-14T18:39:24Z", "timestamp": 1786732764112, "version": "build-2736575974"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The study is attempting to analyse the impacts of AI-driven portfolio optimisation enhancing the data quality and automating workflows. The AI is being increasingly used for investment decisions and businesses can benefit through their adoption. The study has strived to address the gap by analysing influences on workflow and data quality. The study reveals how workflow is benefitted through the adoption of AI. However, the data quality is often compromised and there can be flawed results. The training of models is required to gain accurate results that can mitigate risks.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.5278219", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 3]], "date-time": "2025-06-03T14:25:34Z", "timestamp": 1748960734000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["AI-DRIVEN PORTFOLIO OPTIMIZATION ENHANCING DATA QUALITY AND AUTOMATING WORKFLOWS 2023"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"given": "Anusha", "family": "Nerella", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 14]], "date-time": "2026-08-14T18:13:56Z", "timestamp": 1786731236000}, "score": 30.130093, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=5278219"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.5278219", "published": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 13]], "date-time": "2025-12-13T07:00:59Z", "timestamp": 1765609259591, "version": "3.48.0"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "ScienceTech Xplore", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["AIJCST"], "DOI": "10.63282/3117-5481/aijcst-v4i6p101", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 13]], "date-time": "2025-12-13T06:51:43Z", "timestamp": 1765608703000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["The Role of Generative AI in Transforming Data Engineering Workflows and Automating Computational Infrastructure Design"], "prefix": "10.63282", "volume": "4", "author": [{"given": "Ayaka", "family": "Hasegawa", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Hinata", "family": "Shimizu", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "52640", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2022]]}, "container-title": ["American International Journal of Computer Science and Technology"], "link": [{"URL": "https://aijcst.org/index.php/aijcst/article/view/47/40", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 12, 13]], "date-time": "2025-12-13T06:51:45Z", "timestamp": 1765608705000}, "score": 29.957983, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://aijcst.org/index.php/aijcst/article/view/47"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2022]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.63282/3117-5481/aijcst-v4i6p101", "ISSN": ["3117-5481"], "issn-type": [{"value": "3117-5481", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2022]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 13]], "date-time": "2026-01-13T00:29:28Z", "timestamp": 1768264168122, "version": "3.49.0"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "EP-Journals", "issue": "04", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["GJETR"], "abstract": "<jats:p>Reservoir characterization is a critical process in the energy industry, providing insights into subsurface properties essential for efficient exploration, production, and management. Traditional workflows are hindered by inefficiencies in handling diverse datasets, reliance on manual processes, and the challenges of integrating structured and unstructured information. This paper proposes a conceptual framework to automate reservoir characterization workflows by leveraging advanced technologies such as Natural Language Processing (NLP), data integration tools, and visualization systems. The framework encompasses four key components: data acquisition and preprocessing, text analysis through NLP models, a robust integration layer for harmonizing datasets, and intuitive visualization tools for enhanced decision-making. The framework aims to improve efficiency, accuracy, and collaboration in reservoir studies by automating and streamlining these processes. The paper also discusses the anticipated benefits, including faster decision-making and greater insight, alongside challenges such as computational demands, data quality issues, and the need for domain-specific model customization. Strategies to mitigate these challenges and recommendations for future research and practical implementation are proposed. This framework represents a transformative approach, offering a scalable solution to modernize reservoir characterization and drive innovation in the energy sector.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.65150/ep-gjetr/v1e4/2025-09", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 12]], "date-time": "2026-01-12T19:14:29Z", "timestamp": 1768245269000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["A Conceptual Framework for Automating Reservoir Characterization Workflows Using NLP and Data Integration"], "prefix": "10.65150", "volume": "01", "author": [{"name": "Schlumberger Oilfield UK Ltd, UK", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Lymmy", "family": "Ogbidi", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Benneth", "family": "Oteh", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"name": "TotalEnergies Exploration and Production Kampala, Uganda", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "54641", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2026, 12, 31]]}, "container-title": ["Global Journal of Engineering and Technology Research"], "original-title": ["A Conceptual Framework for Automating Reservoir Characterization Workflows Using NLP and Data Integration"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 12]], "date-time": "2026-01-12T19:14:30Z", "timestamp": 1768245270000}, "score": 29.639784, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://gjetr.ep-journals.org/index.php/gjetr/article/view/33"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026, 12, 31]]}, "references-count": 0, "journal-issue": {"issue": "04", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2026, 12, 31]]}},